{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday","id":1540220,"title":"Fire & Revolution: Carthians (Coming Wednesday!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-12T13:52:05-07:00","id":1540220,"title":"Fire & Revolution: Carthians (Coming Wednesday!)","content":"Edit: Get it here! <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a><br /> <br /> Hello again! Time to break out the Little Red Book once more.<br /> <br /> Some of you who follow the doings of None More Dark Publishing might know that we have a covenant book for <b>Vampire: The Requiem Second Edition</b> in the works: <b>Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</b>. Well, I\u2019m here to tell you it\u2019s coming next week as a little late-summer gift to all you CofD fans (i.e., Wednesday, August 14th). At 12 PST, that\u2019ll be dropping on DTRPG and the Storytellers Vault. We had wanted to drop this in July, but sadly, we had some delays, but we're basically ready to go now!<br /> <br /> If you don\u2019t know who/what NMD is, we\u2019re a collective of RPG authors and artists who\u2019ve spent the last three-ish years creating supplements for <b>Requiem</b>. Because the current IP owner has stopped approving new official releases for the Chronicles of Darkness (to the best of my knowledge; I have no other information in that regard beyond what everyone else has seen), we\u2019ve been trying to carry the torch, at least with <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Changeling</b>.<br /> <br /> So, what\u2019s in this book? Let me quote the back cover. <b>Fire &amp; Revolution </b>includes:<ul><li>A complete guide to the Carthians, reformists of the All Night Society.</li> <li>Concordats, factions, and ghoul families, ready to light up the world on the Revolution\u2019s behalf.</li> <li>New Archetypes, Devotions, and Merits; optional mechanics for debates, elections, and improvised Carthian Law; and errata for systems in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>.</li> <li>Radical schisms and reactionary horrors, including the return of the Commonwealth, the Movement\u2019s sinister globe-spanning shadow.</li> </ul>Why do covenant books if we have <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>? Well, as cool as <b>SotC </b>is, it's a very specific kind of book. I wanted to provide something a bit more big-picture. I also wanted to cover more systems than <b>SotC </b>had the space for. Plus, <b>SotC </b>is getting close to 9 years old now, and I think it's worthwhile to provide the covenants with a fresh coat of paint.<br /> <br /> The other reason was that everyone really wanted us to do covenant books, and we're not ones to fly in the face of public opinion!<br /> <br /> We started with the Carthians mostly because of alphabetical order, but I also felt they needed the most work in terms of adjusting popular perceptions. The Firebrands sometimes get painted with a, shall we say... Anarch brush that I don't care for. The Carthians aren't Anarchs (the Carthians aren't even <i>really </i>based on the Anarchs), and they're not even always left-wing. I think some folks read them as kinda default progressives (in human terms), and while that's true in contrast to the Invictus \u2014 everything is progressive compared with feudal gerontocracy \u2014 the Movement has a much sharper edge than &quot;vague vampire socialism.&quot; At least to me, the Movement is more compelling (and weird) if it's ideologically diverse. All that said, the idea of the Movement being Revolutionary yet the wielders of literal Law has sometimes stuck in people's craws. I don't think there's really a contradiction there, but I see why folks sometimes perceive one; thus, I wanted to really dig into dispelling that perception.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to get away from the idea that the Carthians are the good vampires. Some Carthians certainly try to be the lesser of five evils when it comes to the human equation, but the Carthian <i>Movement </i>(at least the way we conceive it) doesn't give one whit about humanity other than as a source of ideology. Do all Firebrands agree with that? Definitely not! And that's a dramatic angle for you to explore.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll get into the specifics more in the coming week (like how this book relates to <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b> and why we chose to do it), but for now, I\u2019ll leave you with a short preview of our big system innovation in this book: <b>concordats</b>.<br /> <br /> On Monday I\u2019ll be back with another preview. What would you like: A concordat or some new Carthian Laws? Or should I talk about the Commonwealth...?<br /> <br /> Also, I hasten to noted that NMD has a Patreon: <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/NoneMoreDarkPublishing\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/NoneMoreDarkPublishing</a>. There are already a bunch of Carthian previews on there, and most of them are available for free supporters. We\u2019re going to be adding some new tiers and content soon!<br /> <br /> So, if you'd like to support us in other ways than just buying our books, we'll have more about that soon.<br /> <br /> <b>Concordats</b><br /> <br /> Covenants are pacts made in Vitae. Most Kindred take this as a social contract, but in truth, this promise is also sealed in the Curse, though it\u2019s hard to say when or where. Not all sects of the Damned are true covenants of the Blood, and while that might seem like a fine distinction, covenants can employ \u201cpractices\u201d minor gangs of Kindred can\u2019t. These include Carthian Law, the Coils of the Dragon, Invictus Oaths, and the various forms of blood sorcery \u2014 but there are other perks as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Concordats </b>are one of these perks. Similar to bloodlines, these are fraternal groups the dead can forge, albeit based on political or religious persuasion rather than family ties. Like covenants in miniature, they\u2019re dedicated to a particular purpose, albeit narrower than those of the five great sects. As such, concordats are rarer than true bloodlines; many Kindred can\u2019t tell the difference, and considering the mutable qualities of the Blood, some may have even become true lineages over the years.<br /> <br /> Concordats are less defined than bloodlines. They\u2019re more like templates that get passed from city to city, sometimes dissolving when they feel they\u2019ve fulfilled their vows. A few have more storied histories, especially in local settings, and some have been reformed through spontaneous invention. They might even have different names depending on where they operate, though they tend to share a common one. They\u2019re also not unified by any particular ideology beyond what their local covenant has set down.<br /> <br /> In theory, they\u2019re functional, not political, working for the good of all members of the covenant. In practice, it\u2019s more complicated than that. Concordats can attain a great deal of power even beyond their factions, but they\u2019re also bound by their vows, and if they move against their comrades for selfish reasons, they lose access to their special abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> A vampire joining a concordat needs a dot of Covenant Status and a willing <b>Fidelis </b>(see below). Any member can act as Fidelis if she has higher Blood Potency than the initiate. The only other restriction is that a vampire cannot be part of a \u201ctrue\u201d bloodline when she joins or forms a concordat.<br /> <br /> Concordats are open to all clans. A handful may restrict membership to certain Kindred families for political or social reasons, but none are supernaturally restrictive (that anyone knows of).<br /> <br /> A character can only have one concordat at a time, though nothing says she can\u2019t join another at a later time.<br /> <br /> <b>The Vow</b><br /> <br /> Concordats are always created with a purpose in mind, something that can only be accomplished by twisting the Blood so much that it creates a mystic link with their covenant. This purpose is called a <b>vow</b>, similar to both a bane and a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> A concordat member must follow her vow to the best of her ability. Fulfilling it and incurring a breaking point before the end of the night grants a +2 on detachment and an additional Beat. However, breaking it instead applies a \u20132 on detachment and grants no Beat for risking Humanity. These effects apply once per night; if a character fulfills and then violates her vow, or vice versa, the most recent action applies to any breaking point.<br /> <br /> A vow must be feasible and can\u2019t be inherently fatal: A concordat can\u2019t vow to sunbathe,. Vows are also usually open-ended, but some are time-sensitive, sworn only to deal with grave emergencies. The Storyteller adjudicates all ambiguities, and she\u2019s free to make decisions based on a given character\u2019s personal beliefs.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b><br /> <br /> When a vampire joins a concordat, she replaces one common Discipline in her clan spread with two new powers associated with each group: a common one (Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate, Resilience, or Vigor) and a signature one (Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, or Protean). The player chooses which common Discipline to replace. If a vampire already favors one of these powers, she gains a Discipline of the player\u2019s choice as an alternative, though it must be from the same category (common or clan). If she favors both Disciplines, she gains an additional clan power.<br /> <br /> For example, a Daeva Red Eye (p. XX) gains Auspex and Resilience. Her player drops Vigor, leaving her with Auspex, Celerity, Majesty, and Resilience. Conversely, a Mekhet recruit gains Resilience, and because he already favors Auspex, his player decides to replace Celerity with Dominate.<br /> <br /> Concordats never gain access to unique Disciplines like Cachexy, Crochan, Dead Signal, etc. These are the province of true bloodlines. However, concordats in the Circle of the Crone, Lancea et Sanctum, Architects of the Monolith, and other covenants with access to blood sorcery can bestow Ritual Disciplines as favored powers, though their vows are stricter.<br /> <br /> <b>Gift</b><br /> <br /> Concordats always gain an inherent supernatural gift, the effect of which increases as a vampire gains Kindred Status in her covenant. This gift is loosely tied to the concordat\u2019s vow, at the very least providing members an advantage in keeping it. Concordats can sometimes access special Devotions or Merits, but unlike bloodlines, these aren\u2019t always exclusive to the group.<br /> <br /> <b>Creating a Concordat</b><br /> <br /> To form a concordat, a vampire in good standing with her covenant must make the concordat\u2019s vow to a character with five dots of Kindred Status in the same faction; in cities without such characters, concordats in that covenant aren\u2019t possible. If this is a concordat of her own design, she must have Blood Potency 5. If it exists elsewhere or previously did so in the city, she only needs Blood Potency 3, but she must have tasted the blood of a former/current member or have a blood tie to one. She must also have five dots of the concordat\u2019s favored unique power at at least a dot of its common one.<br /> <br /> Once the vow is agreed upon, the high-ranking vampire sacrifices a Humanity dot, and the other sacrifices a Blood Potency dot. The latter serves as the concordat\u2019s first Fidelis, the equivalent of an Avus. A vampire cannot make a vow to herself.<br /> <br /> The first Fidelis has no power over her concordat beyond the blood bonds she might form with converts. If she dies or falls to torpor, the concordat won\u2019t end, as she\u2019s a political leader, not a mystical one. As long as one member of the concordat exists, they can pass on their vow.<br /> <br /> <b>Breaking the Pact</b><br /> <br /> Concordats are indefinite groupings, not permanent ones. If a vampire joins a true bloodline or sheds her last Covenant Status dot, she incurs detachment at Humanity 2 as if she had broken her vow; succeed or fail, she\u2019s no longer a member. Her affinity powers revert or change as appropriate, and she\u2019s no longer bound by the concordat\u2019s vow. She keeps any Disciplines she purchased at a cost break, but she loses that discount and can no longer access the concordat\u2019s gift. She keeps any Merits or Devotions except abilities that tie into that gift; Sanctity of Merits applies, and lost Devotions are refunded in Experiences.<br /> <br /> A concordat can voluntarily disband. If a majority of members in the city agree and spill a Vitae each in a short ceremony, they can declare their vow fulfilled. They lose all benefits as described above, but they suffer no breaking points.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-14-2024, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T20:30:35-07:00","id":1540258,"title":"","content":"Here we go!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T04:03:54-07:00","id":1540266,"title":"","content":"Do you do anything special when a vampire's discipline affinities shift? Is there a penalty to a discipline that was bought at the reduced rate but is now out-of-clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T05:54:40-07:00","id":1540269,"title":"","content":"Damn it. One more NMD book to buy soonish it seems. And I need to print the ones I own someday to better read them haha !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T06:57:43-07:00","id":1540271,"title":"","content":"This looks interesting and in particular that the Carthians are expanded beyond socialists. I can't say that I'll get it right on release but I hope to get it eventually.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I would hope there's some discussion of ideology and how that might be moved into the Kindred existance. Here's me hoping at least a discussion on socialism and liberalism as these might translate to the vampire existance. And if more ideologies gets included, all the more interesting both to run Carthians as more diverse as well as running them as the bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T13:01:20-07:00","id":1540283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540266#post1540266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you do anything special when a vampire's discipline affinities shift? Is there a penalty to a discipline that was bought at the reduced rate but is now out-of-clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you just lose that power as an affinity, so it's not as cheap. If you later left the concordat, you'd regain it (there's probably ways one could game this system a bit, but that's the kind of thing where I leave it to Storytellers to deal with bad-faith players).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T13:10:21-07:00","id":1540286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540271#post1540271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the meantime, I would hope there's some discussion of ideology and how that might be moved into the Kindred existance. Here's me hoping at least a discussion on socialism and liberalism as these might translate to the vampire existance. And if more ideologies gets included, all the more interesting both to run Carthians as more diverse as well as running them as the bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of! We initially set out to talk about the ins and outs of vampire socialism/liberalism/conservatism/etc. in first drafts, but what we ended up with was, frankly, rather boring, and ultimately not that different from what you might read in a Wikipedia article (turns out you can change &quot;money&quot; to &quot;blood&quot; and cover a lot of Kindred political economies without much heavy lifting).<br /> <br /> Instead, we talk about Carthian appropriation of human ideologies in more practical terms, with five example &quot;experiments&quot;. For example, we have one called The Welfare State, which uses a social democratic model, and another called The Impartial Meritocracy, which is pretty much what it sounds like. We also have one called The Uneasy Compromise, which is effectively the default Carthian domain. In ideological terms, we talk more about how Carthians differ in changing the All Night Society rather than where they fall on the left and right. We also include several factions, which are very diverse ideologically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T14:26:29-07:00","id":1540296,"title":"","content":"You planning to do anything with the Sunwalker Knights? Not that I'd necessarily use it, but I'd love to see it. I have had a chronicle in which it happened, and some other loosely connected chronicles in which it was part of the background that it had happened, in which the Knights successfully infested most Carthians, which was regarded as a win by 90% of Knights - everyone but soreheads who wanted their own club more than they wanted to get their message out - and by many Carthians outside Radical Collectivists, for whom it is obviously total poison. Oh, and they brought in the Kallisti, who pay essentially <i>nothing </i>to have their shadows washed, and of course make excellent &quot;deprogrammers.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I decided not to give the Kallisti an extra problem for Washing the Shadow, or bar them from using it. I decided that sometimes a real free thing shows up, and when it does you'd be a fool not to take it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T14:46:29-07:00","id":1540298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540296#post1540296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You planning to do anything with the Sunwalker Knights? Not that I'd necessarily use it, but I'd love to see it. I have had a chronicle in which it happened, and some other loosely connected chronicles in which it was part of the background that it had happened, in which the Knights successfully infested most Carthians, which was regarded as a win by 90% of Knights - everyone but soreheads who wanted their own club more than they wanted to get their message out - and by many Carthians outside Radical Collectivists, for whom it is obviously total poison. Oh, and they brought in the Kallisti, who pay essentially <i>nothing </i>to have their shadows washed, and of course make excellent &quot;deprogrammers.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I decided not to give the Kallisti an extra problem for Washing the Shadow, or bar them from using it. I decided that sometimes a real free thing shows up, and when it does you'd be a fool not to take it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We're considering bringing the Sun-Walking Knights in for the Ordo Dracul book, but that'll be a while yet. I want to see if I can get all the <b>TDM </b>covenants into Second Edition, and I THINK I'm about halfway through now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T14:49:11-07:00","id":1540299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540298#post1540298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're considering bringing the Sun-Walking Knights in for the Ordo Dracul book, but that'll be a while yet. I want to see if I can get all the <b>TDM </b>covenants into Second Edition, and I THINK I'm about halfway through now...</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, as I say, I'd love to see it.<br /> <br /> TDM is in an interesting position, it's kind of V:tR 1.5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T14:59:41-07:00","id":1540301,"title":"","content":"Alphabetically, Ordo Dracul is dead last, isn't it? Damn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T15:02:36-07:00","id":1540302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540301#post1540301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alphabetically, Ordo Dracul is dead last, isn't it? Damn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're easily my favourite, but I wanted to not be arbitrary about the order like I was with the clan books. That said, we'll have learned a lot from doing four of these beforehand, so the ORdo should get a really, REALLY good book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T15:07:00-07:00","id":1540303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540302#post1540302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, they're easily my favourite, but I wanted to not be arbitrary about the order like I was with the clan books. That said, we'll have learned a lot from doing four of these beforehand, so the ORdo should get a really, REALLY good book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rough with the smooth, I'll take it. Really appreciate your operation, even if I don't always agree. May I compliment you on simplified Crochan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T15:44:30-07:00","id":1540306,"title":"","content":"Had a Prince once, who had been in the Ordo Dracul until he quit for the Invictus, Like many elders, he was frozen in time, but the time he was frozen in was the Enlightenment, and he was big for the marketplace of ideas. He leaned on the local Academy hard to teach the first tier of the Coil of Blood (this was 1e) for nothing. He laid it out for them. &quot;It benefits everyone. You get to assess interest and aptitude. Others learn that you have no secrets to be stolen - it's a demanding process, to which you have to commit. And finally, and most importantly, it's your Black Rent, and you don't really have a choice.&quot; He also had this thing where he didn't care if Covenant leaders were pure conduits for their constituency or had their constituency under their thumb - but if they didn't manifestly have <i>one </i>of those, they lost the exclusive right to speak.<br /> Also he had what appeared to be a buzz-cut, and it was not generally known that when he stopped living that had been meant to go under a powdered wig.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-13-2024, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T16:34:27-07:00","id":1540309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540303#post1540303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rough with the smooth, I'll take it. Really appreciate your operation, even if I don't always agree. May I compliment you on simplified Crochan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'm really happy with how we updated Crochan. I'd love to do a modern version of the Bron one day that includes those rules in write-up rather than an appendix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T12:03:48-07:00","id":1540376,"title":"","content":"Now available!!<br /> <br /> The book: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a><br /> Clan bundle: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491575/Clans-of-the-Revolution-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a><br /> Bloodline bundle: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491571/Blood-of-the-Revolution-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a><br /> Rome bundle: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491579/Rome-and-the-Revolution-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a><br /> Changeling bundle: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491577/Fire-and-Thorns-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...iate_id=321925</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T12:30:37-07:00","id":1540378,"title":"","content":"Alright, now that I've had a chance to spam the link everywhere, let's look at the <b>Guillotines</b>.<br /> <br /> Concordats, at least from a design perspective, are meant to be task-oriented, and oh boy do the Guillotines have a task. Carthians don't choose violence as a matter of course (at least officially), but when they do choose violence, they don't screw around.<br /> <br /> The Guillotines are who the Carthians call on when they face an existential threat or an enemy vile enough that the only answer is Final Death. They &quot;charge&quot; themselves with the blood of their comrades and gain terrible power for a short time to achieve this purpose. Does this make them ticking timebombs who might just diablerize the entire local Movement if pushed to the edge? Definitely, probably not.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Guillotines! Feel free to ask about the book or let us know what you think! And please consider leaving a star rating and/or a review! It's super helpful for word of mouth. I'll be back tomorrow with another excerpt!<br /> <br /> <b>Guillotines: Blades of the Revolution</b><br /> <br /> <i>I\u2019ll make it quick.</i><br /> <br /> Executioners have a certain mystique. The black-hooded figure might belong more to fiction than reality, but he conjures a palpable aura of fear, of the ultimate authority of the government. While long used to make citizens submissive, during the French Revolution, executions turned into a symbol of the people\u2019s justice, and the infamous guillotine became famous worldwide. The vampires who bear its name perform a similar function: They bring justice to the most wicked Kindred \u2014 and only the Carthian Movement is objective enough to decide who\u2019s deserving of such punishment. Of course.<br /> <br /> In its early nights, the Movement comprised, in its vast majority, young vampires, barely a few decades removed from their mortal lives. This issue persists to this night, with the covenant\u2019s membership skewing younger than most others. Unfortunately for them, age often means power in the All Night Society, and not just the abstract kind. When the Revolution stormed the streets of Paris, the guillotine became a symbol of equality before the law, killing all in the same quick and efficient way. But vampires faced a different challenge: While a mortal king dies as easily as anyone else, a prince can throw would-be assailants through brick walls or move at the speed of thought. This required some of the lateral thinking the Firebrands would later become famous for.<br /> <br /> More extreme wings of the covenant first advocated for diablerie as a quick route to power, but such voices were in the minority, and their experiments led to catastrophic results. What eventually bore fruit was a stopgap measure: selecting willing Kindred to feed on the Vitae of their fellows in large amounts, not draining any single vampire but drinking well above what one could normally consume. After trial and error, this enabled the Blood of the strongest one to adapt, allowing them to temporarily increase the ease Vitae could empower their physical forms. Drenched in gore and bringing equality to the masses, this survivor and their successors named themselves the Guillotines.<br /> <br /> The Executioners bring weight to Carthian threats. Their identities are often unknown even within the covenant, a secret weapon to be deployed only against the highest-profile targets. Despite their name, they rarely perform public executions, as capturing and keeping powerful Kindred on ice is both difficult and dangerous. Rather, they strike their targets where they ought to feel safe, employing a mix of Protean and daring to access them.<br /> <br /> The Guillotines pride themselves on avoiding needless pain in their duties: A strong killing blow to the neck or head is their preferred method of delivering Final Death. They often leave a sign of their presence though, like the Carthian crest or the image of a guillotine, so the masses know who delivered justice.<br /> <br /> Using the Guillotines is a last resort, as their methods pose several issues. Sooner or later, most become addicted to Vitae, and either blood-bound to most covenant members or in thrall to a single one, tangling them in complex emotional webs and reducing their loyalties to the Movement itself. And a Requiem of gorging on Vitae and murdering powerful vampires does little to keep the Beast in check, so most Guillotines who survive for any significant amount of time end up victims of powerful banes, less and less able to relate to mortals. The thought of a Guillotine draugr, driven to ruin by a hunger for Vitae they can never satisfy, is enough to keep even the most fanatical Carthians from calling upon them too easily.<br /> <br /> <b>How we serve</b><br /> <br /> When an enemy of the people must fall, we\u2019re the ones to answer the call. We gorge ourselves on the blood of our fellow Firebrands, and for one night, we revel in the kind of power others wait centuries to obtain. The look on the face of an ancient terror when it\u2019s felled by someone a fraction of its age is one you\u2019ll <i>never </i>get enough of.<br /> <br /> <b>How we dissent</b><br /> <br /> Being a weapon can be frustrating if you remain sheathed for too long. Our duty is to the Movement, and it picks our targets, but staying inactive for too long can feel\u2026 <i>itchy</i>. And how quick our leaders are to forget us once they\u2019re the ones in power. They should do well to remember a blade cuts both ways.<br /> <br /> <b>Concordat Origins</b><ul><li>\u201cTo arms, citizens!\u201d echoed the cries of the French masses. In the nights of the Revolution, as the name E. B. Carth and <i>Contre les vampires patriarcaux</i> spread like wildfire and before the Movement that bears his name came together, a few desperate neonates chose one of their own to become the living weapon of their revolt, a blade that would cut down those who had dared violate the rights of the people. He carved a bloody path through the nights of Paris, eliminating tyrants who thought themselves unassailable for centuries. Le Guillotineur, as he was called, remained active throughout the days of the First French Empire and disappeared shortly after, but he had several apprentices and inspired many more. However, the fact that no record of his Final Death exists is of concern to some. How dangerous could an elder Executioner be?</li> <li>It happened in a Brazilian city around the dawn of the 20th century. Some say Rio, or S\u00e3o Paolo, while others say it was somewhere far less important. It started as a beautiful example of Carthian revolution, the destruction of the entire Sanctified ruling class and the founding of a new order. But it didn\u2019t go according to plan. The new \u201cColonel\u201d styled herself a military dictator and enforced her rule through a brutal militia. She became crueler and more twisted with each passing night, to the point where vampires felt they had less power now than ever before. Something had to be done, and a small coterie of neonates uncovered the means to become Executioners. They fed on each other, forming a tangle of Vincula, and unleashed their revenge on the leaders who had betrayed the Revolution. Suspicion and murders only enhanced the Colonel\u2019s paranoia, and the Movement crumbled around her, with the Invictus moving in to fill the gap \u2014 with their first official action burning the Executioners to ashes. Liberty or Final Death, indeed.</li> <li>The Executioners are older than the Movement, or even guillotines for that matter. Ever heard the expression \u201cavenging angel?\u201d They\u2019re a gift from God. No, they\u2019re not from the Sanctified, either. They <i>predate </i>Longinus, with mentions of them in obscure rabbinical texts and Sumerian tablets, if you know where to look. Only the Revolution can call upon them because it\u2019s the only covenant that fosters true community. Firebrand opinions about religion vary (like everything, some might say) but Carthians are the only Licks who consider the group, not just the individual. So, when things are dire, God \u2014 or Gaia, or the Curse, or whatever you want to call it \u2014 chooses some to become instruments of retribution. Sure, they have to hasten the process with Vitae, but what deity doesn\u2019t ask for a little sacrifice? Everything has a price\u2026 and the Guillotines might not yet know what it is for their particular gift.</li> </ul><b>Nicknames: </b>Executioners, Butchers (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Concordat Vow (The Pledge of Restraint): </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:04:29-07:00","id":1540445,"title":"","content":"Hey, I got the book, and it is amazing. I have a question, how does Bullet Time and Quicken Sight compares narratively? They both sounds kind of the same power with different mechanics that stack with each other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:27:49-07:00","id":1540456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540445#post1540445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I got the book, and it is amazing. I have a question, how does Bullet Time and Quicken Sight compares narratively? They both sounds kind of the same power with different mechanics that stack with each other</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullet Time is more about boosting and adjusting your reflexive reaction speed without any mental effort, whereas Quicken Sight gives you a greater sense of awareness such that the world seems to slow down for a moment. For example, you can't use Bullet Time to read quickly. Glad you're enjoying the book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T17:20:01-07:00","id":1540480,"title":"","content":"My typical questions coming up<br /> <br /> 1. Favorite and most difficult section to write for the book? Along with your favorite antagonist?<br /> <br /> 2. Was there any big changes made during the process of creating this book? What aspect were you looking to emphasize, and what were you looking to not acknowledge at all (or view of the covenant you wished to dispel? Though I feel you already answered that with the popular &quot;good vampires&quot; belief around the carthians)<br /> <br /> 3. Favorite covenant?<br /> <br /> 4. how will this book influence Circle of the Crone? What lessons have you learned making this book that will directly effect the next? Basically, what I'm asking is will you approach the next covenant books differently after the learning experience of this one?<br /> <br /> Also as an aside, I realize you're not alone in this book, but i dont want to bother them with the same questions unless theyd like to answer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:17:27-07:00","id":1540488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540480#post1540480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My typical questions coming up<br /> <br /> 1. Favorite and most difficult section to write for the book? Along with your favorite antagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first chapter was a challenge, because it was mostly storytelling and player advice, and it's tricky to do those well without being dry. As for antagonists, I really like the Commonwealth of the two schisms (even though I wrote the other one, haha), and the hidebound are probably my favourite of the horrors, though they're all great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Was there any big changes made during the process of creating this book? What aspect were you looking to emphasize, and what were you looking to not acknowledge at all (or view of the covenant you wished to dispel? Though I feel you already answered that with the popular &quot;good vampires&quot; belief around the carthians) </div> </div> </div>This one went through some growing pains. What I had in the outline is a lot different from what we ended up with, especially that first chapter.<br /> <br /> Aside from dispelling the &quot;good vampires&quot; misconception, I wanted to present the Movement as more ideologically diverse than they sometimes get credit for. I think the closer they are to fitting into a particular human political ideology every time, the less interesting they are. That meant countering the stereotype that they're always left-wing in human terms. I also very much wanted to do away with the idea that the Carthians are just the <b>Requiem </b>version of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> We didn't really avoid talking about anything, I don't think!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Favorite covenant? </div> </div> </div>Definitely the Ordo Dracul, followed closely by the Sanctified and the Carthians sharing second place. I really like the Invictus, but I think in my mind they're kind of default vampires, which isn't really true, but that's just where my brain slots them in. I <i>like </i>the Circle of the Crone, but they're often my last choice as a player.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. how will this book influence Circle of the Crone? What lessons have you learned making this book that will directly effect the next? Basically, what I'm asking is will you approach the next covenant books differently after the learning experience of this one? </div> </div> </div>I suspect the Crone book will be patterned off this one pretty significantly, since the Acolytes are the other &quot;progressive&quot; faction in the progressive/conservative\u2013secular/spiritual dichotomy that the covenants have going (at least the ones that aren't the Dragons...but we'll get to that). That probably means that the Invictus and Sanctified books will form their own pair, and then the Dragons get to be on their own weird Z-axis.<br /> <br /> In general though, I think I'm going to make sure I'm happy with the outline before I dig too deep. Looking back, it was a little underbaked, and that led to the book taking longer than I wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also as an aside, I realize you're not alone in this book, but i dont want to bother them with the same questions unless theyd like to answer </div> </div> </div>I don't think most of the authors are on here, but they're welcome to answer anything relevant if they come across this post!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T06:16:41-07:00","id":1540506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540488#post1540488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think most of the authors are on here, but they're welcome to answer anything relevant if they come across this post!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm here! I wrote the Commonwealth, so I'm happy to answer any questions relating to them, as well as receive constructive criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T10:30:22-07:00","id":1540514,"title":"","content":"I'm also here! I wrote a bunch of Merits and one of the concordats [the Macrina, specifically].<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540480#post1540480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Favorite and most difficult section to write for the book? Along with your favorite antagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't feel qualified to answer your other questions, I think I can give this one a shot!<br /> <br /> I have a ton of fun writing little globs of character customization, like Merits [and Devotions, but I didn't write any in this book], however I think in the end the Macrina are my favorite contribution. They just were also the hardest for me to write! I'm a lot more comfortable writing rules than I am writing prose, so there were a lot of times I struggled finding the right words to communicate my ideas without rambling \u2014 or worse, being boring. However, I think I managed to capture the voice I was looking for well enough in the end! And the Macrina are just so <i>nasty</i> [affectionate], I love them!<br /> <br /> And my favorite antagonist is also the Commonwealth, though I admit I haven't read about MOCSY in much detail yet. I do think it's neat we appear to have snuck a Contagion in there, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Favorite covenant? </div> </div> </div>Well, I <i>am</i> an Acolyte Apologist...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T12:14:22-07:00","id":1540584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540514#post1540514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also here! I wrote a bunch of Merits and one of the concordats [the Macrina, specifically].<br /> <br /> <br /> While I don't feel qualified to answer your other questions, I think I can give this one a shot!<br /> <br /> I have a ton of fun writing little globs of character customization, like Merits [and Devotions, but I didn't write any in this book], however I think in the end the Macrina are my favorite contribution. They just were also the hardest for me to write! I'm a lot more comfortable writing rules than I am writing prose, so there were a lot of times I struggled finding the right words to communicate my ideas without rambling \u2014 or worse, being boring. However, I think I managed to capture the voice I was looking for well enough in the end! And the Macrina are just so <i>nasty</i> [affectionate], I love them!<br /> <br /> And my favorite antagonist is also the Commonwealth, though I admit I haven't read about MOCSY in much detail yet. I do think it's neat we appear to have snuck a Contagion in there, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I <i>am</i> an Acolyte Apologist...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for taking the time to answer! Honestly the Macrina was my favorite carthian Concordat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T16:53:27-07:00","id":1540595,"title":"","content":"Oh, what was something yall had wanted to put in but had to cut out?<br /> <br /> Also, were concordats a way to more easily envision bloodlines that are within a covenant framework? I understand they have not retconned covenant specific bloodlines, as those still exist within the context of originating in such covenants, but it does seem to be an answer to those who struggle to reconcile a bloodline being so intertwined with a covenant rather than clan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T18:36:29-07:00","id":1540602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540595#post1540595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, what was something yall had wanted to put in but had to cut out?<br /> <br /> Also, were concordats a way to more easily envision bloodlines that are within a covenant framework? I understand they have not retconned covenant specific bloodlines, as those still exist within the context of originating in such covenants, but it does seem to be an answer to those who struggle to reconcile a bloodline being so intertwined with a covenant rather than clan</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much exactly it. A sidebar got cut that talks a bit about this, actually, but in essence, concordats are for anyone who wants to have covenant bloodlines but doesn't like the framework they're presented in. In <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected</b>, we include a sidebar talking about how you might run the Parliamentarian bloodline as a concordat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T23:49:47-07:00","id":1540610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540506#post1540506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm here! I wrote the Commonwealth, so I'm happy to answer any questions relating to them, as well as receive constructive criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I didn't see this earlier lol<br /> <br /> I'll have to re-read them to have what I hope would be good constructive criticisms (just finished the book), but some questions i have regards the creative process you took with them. In order to reconcile existing within the Carthian Movement, you have seemed to given them somewhat of a &quot;red scare&quot; theme. Is this intentional? I quite like it, especially since it doubles as a pun. 2nd, how do you (or how would you) intend to run them in your settings in terms of scale? In general, is it fair to assume they have a fair amount of small experimental cities set up, or are even these so few as to be special edge cases each? 3rd, unlike the AOA, the Commonwealth has quite a lot of mechanical exceptions from the Movement while still being part of it. Was this something you had in mind from the start, or was there more to it. 4th, how was the experience re-introducing this group to the game?<br /> <br /> Oh, and who made the art for it? I love it<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just an aside, what do you think of the Parlimentarians <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>? Personally I actually quite like them as a bloodline, though i do think ill be having their origins as a concordat that became a bloodline later down the line","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 08-18-2024, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T09:25:10-07:00","id":1540632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540610#post1540610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to reconcile existing within the Carthian Movement, you have seemed to given them somewhat of a &quot;red scare&quot; theme. Is this intentional? I quite like it, especially since it doubles as a pun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really go out of my way to play up the Red Scare. Rather, that happened pretty naturally. The original in The Danse Macabre isn't aesthetically styled after stalinism, but it has all the hallmarks of it: Authoritarian socialism with enforced ideological purity. It's Soviet at its absolute worst, and I was directed to lean into that. So how do I turn that into a group that could believably coexist (if by necessity rather than choice) with all the other Covenants?<br /> <br /> Simply put, they just can't be open about their true nature and goals. In the biggest break from the TDM version (other than turning them into a schism of the Carthians rather than a conspiracy intended to replace them, but that's the premise of including them in this book) I made them careful, because they absolutely need to be in order to survive as a group. They hide, they infiltrate, they recruit through sweet offers of their perceived utopian society. I don't think it's surprising that McCarthy and Hoover (and others) envisioned the Soviets to do the same.<br /> Besides, its already their MO regarding human society. It's kinda natural they do the same in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2nd, how do you (or how would you) intend to run them in your settings in terms of scale? In general, is it fair to assume they have a fair amount of small experimental cities set up, or are even these so few as to be special edge cases each? </div> </div> </div>It really depends on the needs and tone of the game. If it's a paranoid game of politics and intrigue, the Commonwealth might be a big regional power hidden just out of sight, but with probably at most one pilot city for the coterie to stumble upon, ticking perfectly (like a time bomb). A game where the players play Citizens, the entire game might be set in one of them. In most other cases, the Commonwealth might not have any pilot cities, but rather have similar attempts to &quot;live&quot; openly in gated communities or reveal themselves for fully infiltrated organisations as proof-of-concept.<br /> But in most cases, it doesn't really matter how many of these cities the Commonwealth has set up since most games of Vampire doesn't feature a lot of travel. And with the top-down hierarchy of the Commonwealth, it's unlikely most people involved in one of these cities would know about any others, if they exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3rd, unlike the AOA, the Commonwealth has quite a lot of mechanical exceptions from the Movement while still being part of it. Was this something you had in mind from the start, or was there more to it. </div> </div> </div>That's the thing. <i>Is</i> the Commonwealth part of the Movement? It's certainly born from it, but the line between them is intentionally blurred. Whether or not they are separate (if still largely overlapping), the Commonwealth has a very strong identity and hierarchy which definitely sets it apart from (the rest of) the Movement. Which is why a few Merits got some modifications to reflect this. For example, Casual User grants Haven because that's one of the things the Commonwealth explicitly intends to provide for all Kindred once they take power (as their societal duty, so no need to suspect ulterior motives).<br /> <br /> Which is also why Commonwealth Law differs so much from regular Carthian Law. Instead of imposing effects on a domain (as most Carthian Laws do), they empower the individual Citizen to the role they've been given by the Commonwealth. Why/how this works like it does, and whether Commonwealth Law can even be considered a type of Carthian Law or if it's its own thing, would be interesting to explore, but alas, word count. (Originally, the direction was to use Carthian Laws if I wanted to give them a covenant-type advantage, but I quickly got the go-ahead for the current concept of Commonwealth Laws.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4th, how was the experience re-introducing this group to the game? </div> </div> </div>It was fun to turn these guys from gonzo global conspiracy to a more grounded version while still maintaining their extreme goals. I immediately decided on making them competent and insidious, as opposed to the half-baked fanatics that their own writeup in TDM repeatedly states are idiots. After that (and ignoring the blood orgy thing (though it kinda has a successor in one of the Commonwealth Laws)) the rest mostly just fell in place, including things like organizational structure which TDM mostly skipped (most likely because you're expected to run them like Carthians).<br /> <br /> The process was actually quite similar to the Sta-Au which I updated for Bloodlines: The Ageless. Also a group that should've self-imploded in their original version (imo), that I focused on grounding while still maintaining the extremist factor that's a core part of their identity. (Hmm. Is it possible to be &quot;typecast&quot; as a writer? After just two books? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and who made the art for it? I love it </div> </div> </div>You'll have to ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> for that, I'm afraid.\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T11:50:50-07:00","id":1540643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540610#post1540610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and who made the art for it? I love it</div> </div> </div> </div>A friend of ours who's also an CofD/WoD fan and really wanted to be a part of the project! Also did the kiths in <b>Book of Seemings</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540632#post1540632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Hmm. Is it possible to be &quot;typecast&quot; as a writer? After just two books? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Typecast as &quot;good writer.&quot; &lt;3<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T15:25:24-07:00","id":1540806,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> bad at quoting so I'll number it<br /> <br /> 1. Gotcha, So a natural fit that just happened due to their nature rather than a truly altered take<br /> <br /> 2. I see, so pretty modular as usual. I do like the small scale proofs of concept. May be fun to run a hunter game where a traveling cell learns the horrifying truth that regular people have been led to believe it's OK to live side by side with those who consider you a food source.<br /> <br /> 3. oh I like that obscurity to them! That is an angle I embarrassingly missed on my initial reading. As for the differences in Commonwealth to carthian law, that sorta makes it more like the enforcement of the Legion of the dead interestingly enough. Albeit from a lawful systemic role angle rather than lawful persecutor one.<br /> <br /> 4. Love to hear that! It's always cool listening to writers discuss what they enjoyed in the creative process. I for one thought this was a massive improvement (though, personally, i want to see what yall do with the tier 3 versions of Lancea Et Sanctum and Ordo Dracul. The 2 and 1st weakest write ups in my opinion, respectfully. Very excited to see what yall do with them)<br /> <br /> I'll try to come up with a critical question later, I'm not really good at critique so I'll take my time reading them again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T15:31:40-07:00","id":1540807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540643#post1540643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A friend of ours who's also an CofD/WoD fan and really wanted to be a part of the project! Also did the kiths in <b>Book of Seemings</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Typecast as &quot;good writer.&quot; &lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div>Well tell that friend I thought he did awesome work on both books. Also i do have one extremely minor critique, more of a nitpick to the writing. I don't know if it will be of help to the next books so I apologize if it comes off as rude rather than helpful<br /> <br /> I think the book did a real good job of showing us carthians are bastards, same as all other vampires. However, I also feel that there were a fair amount of times the book says some variation of &quot;this may seem good for mortals, but it really isn't&quot;. But i understand this could just be for emphasis, as there was much more of showing us these atrocities in the writing.<br /> <br /> Another questuon i have is im a bit confused. The book mentions that Covenants, being mass blood concordats basically, actually lock out other Covenants from using their abilities. I thought cruac and theban sorcery could be stolen, as well as the Coils of the Dragon simply being a term dragons use as a Covenant searching for vampiric transcendence. I thought all it really did was give you an organization to back you, otherwise any vampire could do research and such to gain coils<br /> <br /> Also, since this is a book of all the Covenants...will VII be having one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T15:48:41-07:00","id":1540808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540807#post1540807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another questuon i have is im a bit confused. The book mentions that Covenants, being mass blood concordats basically, actually lock out other Covenants from using their abilities. I thought cruac and theban sorcery could be stolen, as well as the Coils of the Dragon simply being a term dragons use as a Covenant searching for vampiric transcendence. I thought all it really did was give you an organization to back you, otherwise any vampire could do research and such to gain coils.</div> </div> </div> </div>The covenants <i>aren't </i>concordats writ large; it's more like concordats are covenants writ small, if that makes any sense. We're mostly saying that the covenants are more than social organizations; there's no exclusivity, just <i>supernatural </i>support, whatever you want that to mean; this is very briefly discussed in Dark Eras 2 in a blink-and-you-miss-it sidebar. Like, a coterie of Kindred can't spontaneously create a covenant-level power, but former members might carry old trade secrets with them if they don't get whacked by their former comrades (Laws are kind of exception to this; they all have an implied Status prerequisite unless otherwise specified, so you actually <i>can't </i>steal them by the strictest reading of the rules. And Oaths just work differently than all the other powers in general because you technically don't buy them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, since this is a book of all the Covenants...will VII be having one? </div> </div> </div><i>Maybe</i>, but I'd be more inclined to do them in a bigger book of horrors, if at all. VII is more interesting as a multiple choice antagonist, and we'd have to be really sure of the idea (or ideas) we were presenting.<br /> <br /> But Belial's Brood is definitely on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-20-2024, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T16:07:55-07:00","id":1540809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540808#post1540808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The covenants <i>aren't </i>concordats writ large; it's more like concordats are covenants writ small, if that makes any sense. We're mostly saying that the covenants are more than social organizations; there's no exclusivity, just <i>supernatural </i>support, whatever you want that to mean; this is very briefly discussed in Dark Eras 2 in a blink-and-you-miss-it sidebar. Like, a coterie of Kindred can't spontaneously create a covenant-level power, but former members might carry old trade secrets with them if they don't get whacked by their former comrades (Laws are kind of exception to this; they all have an implied Status prerequisite unless otherwise specified, so you actually <i>can't </i>steal them by the strictest reading of the rules. And Oaths just work differently than all the other powers in general because you technically don't buy them).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Maybe</i>, but I'd be more inclined to do them in a bigger book of horrors, if at all. VII is more interesting as a multiple choice antagonist, and we'd have to be really sure of the idea (or ideas) we were presenting.<br /> <br /> But Belial's Brood is definitely on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Ahh gotcha. My mistake<br /> <br /> 2. I see your point. I just like the continuity of having having a book for them. I'd still expect to be sorta like the last one, perhaps with the rest of the possible mentioned scenarios from the 2nd edition core. I just feel VII didn't get much of anything this edition<br /> <br /> 3. Now THAT is surprising considering their 2nd edition iteration. What brought that about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T16:16:25-07:00","id":1540810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540809#post1540809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2. I see your point. I just like the continuity of having having a book for them. I'd still expect to be sorta like the last one, perhaps with the rest of the possible mentioned scenarios from the 2nd edition core. I just feel VII didn't get much of anything this edition</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say this: I want to do the Betrayed in some way, some day, but more like how the Akhud are in 2E, where they COULD be VII, but they can also just be their own thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540809#post1540809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. Now THAT is surprising considering their 2nd edition iteration. What brought that about?</div> </div> </div> </div>We'd be doing something that marries their 1st and 2nd edition versions. Sort of like the VII book but all the options are <i>explicitly </i>true at the same time. This would probably come after we do the big five, but maybe we can slip them in earlier. We shall see.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T17:05:15-07:00","id":1540813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540810#post1540810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will say this: I want to do the Betrayed in some way, some day, but more like how the Akhud are in 2E, where they COULD be VII, but they can also just be their own thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We'd be doing something that marries their 1st and 2nd edition versions. Sort of like the VII book but all the options are <i>explicitly </i>true at the same time. This would probably come after we do the big five, but maybe we can slip them in earlier. We shall see.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Ahh ok, I know it's quite popular to have a number or even all of them Canon. If I may ask your opinion, we're you to show the multiple canonical option, would the very symbol &quot;VII&quot; have some sort of vampiric mystic foundation? I would find that an interesting option to explore the seemingly innocuous (for lack of better word) yet strange perpetuation of the symbol<br /> <br /> 2. That makes sense. I actually never read the 1st edition version of them. I really enjoyed what I read in Spilled Blood about them. I am intrigued to see how their nature is reconciled in the even loose organization structure I bet they'll have as a covenant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T17:14:03-07:00","id":1540814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540813#post1540813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Ahh ok, I know it's quite popular to have a number or even all of them Canon. If I may ask your opinion, we're you to show the multiple canonical option, would the very symbol &quot;VII&quot; have some sort of vampiric mystic foundation? I would find that an interesting option to explore the seemingly innocuous (for lack of better word) yet strange perpetuation of the symbol</div> </div> </div> </div>That I don't know! The number is ultimately arbitrary, but we could spin a million different reasons for it. It would depend on what angles we took.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540813#post1540813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. That makes sense. I actually never read the 1st edition version of them. I really enjoyed what I read in Spilled Blood about them. I am intrigued to see how their nature is reconciled in the even loose organization structure I bet they'll have as a covenant</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll be pretty different from any of the mainstream covenants. I can't give too much away right now, though our update of <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted </b>will have a little teaser about the direction we're considering.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T17:19:38-07:00","id":1540815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1540814#post1540814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That I don't know! The number is ultimately arbitrary, but we could spin a million different reasons for it. It would depend on what angles we took.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It'll be pretty different from any of the mainstream covenants. I can't give too much away right now, though our update of <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted </b>will have a little teaser about the direction we're considering.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Lol, I just attach way more importance to things than they need lol. I won't be surprised if that angle isn't considered for long if at all.<br /> <br /> 2. I assumed so, and I'll have to buy your bloodline books at some point. I will be cautiously optimistic about it happening. I'm really curious how such a book would look. Plus I like card carrying villains","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_l