ave both free and paid previews!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is sad indeed. Thanks for the link though I'll head that way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T18:44:01-07:00","id":1541314,"title":"","content":"On the note of improvised stuff for the Ordo, I *absolutely* have some ideas in mind for &quot;Experiments&quot; (related to Scales) for the Ordo as their &quot;improvised&quot; system. Will be talking that over with Yoss when we get to that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T20:21:53-07:00","id":1541320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1541314#post1541314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the note of improvised stuff for the Ordo, I *absolutely* have some ideas in mind for &quot;Experiments&quot; (related to Scales) for the Ordo as their &quot;improvised&quot; system. Will be talking that over with Yoss when we get to that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! I don't expect confirmation, but I do think these will be unstable theories that seek to test the limits of aspects of vampirism in a way different from the transcendence they usually seek, such as testing Ghoul Families or the effects of Diablerie on a vampire who's mind is wiped by Dominate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T08:26:34-07:00","id":1541338,"title":"","content":"I have a few questions about the Improvise Carthian law.<br /> <br /> A) A given character may only maintain BP+Carthian Status of Law as the same time. Now with A Deal with Darkness, a given vampire may only maintain BP (or BP + 2 + Specialties) of Pacts / Oaths they are in. For games using both systems in, would you have these limits be separate, or would they overlap somewhat? Perhaps maintaining a Law counting as maintaining a Pact for a vampire? Although a vampire juggling both systems could be quite fun too and so having them have access to more might be good.<br /> <br /> B) Similarly, perhaps allowing Specialties to increase the amount of laws one may hold at a time?<br /> <br /> C) The Law to my understanding is meant to be going alongside (or explicitly in exception to) the laws of the city. Would you intend for a given's domains all the laws to be written out, so that Carthians know alongside what lines they can establish precedents - thus magically giving enforcement to certain parts of the law?<br /> <br /> D) Does that mean Privilege can enact exceptions?<br /> <br /> E) How does the Improvised Law work when the leadership of the city is not Carthian Movement? Can Carthians declare new laws/interpretations? While they might not be official law, they would get enforcement by the Law? While the book gives recourse for a non-Carthian Prince, it still affects everyone else? is this one of those situations of - yeah they can totally declare whatever they want, but if powers that be are competent it might not go down well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T14:47:11-07:00","id":1541361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1541338#post1541338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few questions about the Improvise Carthian law.<br /> <br /> A) A given character may only maintain BP+Carthian Status of Law as the same time. Now with A Deal with Darkness, a given vampire may only maintain BP (or BP + 2 + Specialties) of Pacts / Oaths they are in. For games using both systems in, would you have these limits be separate, or would they overlap somewhat? Perhaps maintaining a Law counting as maintaining a Pact for a vampire? Although a vampire juggling both systems could be quite fun too and so having them have access to more might be good.<br /> <br /> B) Similarly, perhaps allowing Specialties to increase the amount of laws one may hold at a time?<br /> <br /> C) The Law to my understanding is meant to be going alongside (or explicitly in exception to) the laws of the city. Would you intend for a given's domains all the laws to be written out, so that Carthians know alongside what lines they can establish precedents - thus magically giving enforcement to certain parts of the law?<br /> <br /> D) Does that mean Privilege can enact exceptions?<br /> <br /> E) How does the Improvised Law work when the leadership of the city is not Carthian Movement? Can Carthians declare new laws/interpretations? While they might not be official law, they would get enforcement by the Law? While the book gives recourse for a non-Carthian Prince, it still affects everyone else? is this one of those situations of - yeah they can totally declare whatever they want, but if powers that be are competent it might not go down well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take this on since it's largely my writing.<br /> <br /> A) Keep it separate. Improvised Law is the Carthian's Power, Pacts are taking it from others. Similarly, even if you were JUST using A Deal With Darkness, and using the sidebar for Invictus to forge their own Pacts, I'd let them both empower and seek Pacts entirely separately.<br /> <br /> B) As the section on strengthening or weakening Establishing Precedent goes into, increasing the Laws that can be upkept is a perfectly expected way of tuning the power level. If you want to do that with Specialties instead of a given Skill, absolutely go for it.<br /> <br /> C) As in, does it need to coincide with an explicit tome of laws? Depends on the city. I'd imagine in a city run by the crones there are a lot of &quot;implied&quot; laws that are good enough for Precedent to hook onto, but in an Invictus-run city you likely need to go by the book.<br /> <br /> D) What do you mean? Privilege, by its nature, is exceptions, unless I'm misunderstanding what you're asking.<br /> <br /> E) It works normally. If a Carthian is in a position to declare official laws, they can, and then can Establish Precedent around it. If not, they need to forge Precedent around the laws of those in charge (or in opposition to, for Privilege, which might be better thought of as &quot;Rebellion&quot; in cities where Carthians are at odds). Establishing Precedent is meant to be exactly that; you're not creating a new rule, you're explaining what happens when you break/follow one in a specific way.<br /> The basic idea with Establishing Precedent is you take an existing law or rule for the city, then attach the benefit or drawback to it. You can't Establish a Precedent of &quot;Don't kill the prince or else you take aggravated damage&quot; unless the law of the city already says no killing the prince. You can always get MORE specific, though (like the example of &quot;don't kill the prince&quot; when you're just not meant to cause Final Death at all). Privilege, of course, references the existing law but only to say you don't need to worry about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T07:39:04-07:00","id":1541392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1541361#post1541361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ~stuff~</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reply! <br /> <br /> So now I'm trying to get it to be <i>playable. </i>After all, writing out all the rules and laws is... very hard. And also not sure if playable. Especially in places like the UK, where the law has... very long trails of weird edge cases. <br /> <br /> Feeling like for players I should just allow them to make these up, and then we can just check &quot;how feasible is this to be a law already in there?&quot;. Maybe some roll to go with it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T17:09:53-07:00","id":1541418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1540220-fire-revolution-carthians-coming-wednesday?p=1541392#post1541392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the reply!<br /> <br /> So now I'm trying to get it to be <i>playable. </i>After all, writing out all the rules and laws is... very hard. And also not sure if playable. Especially in places like the UK, where the law has... very long trails of weird edge cases.<br /> <br /> Feeling like for players I should just allow them to make these up, and then we can just check &quot;how feasible is this to be a law already in there?&quot;. Maybe some roll to go with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, to be clear, I am talking entirely in-character with this. As an ST, I *absolutely* suggest that you just deal with it as it comes. &quot;Hey ST, is there a law written about trespassing?&quot; when they want to make a no trespassing sign, rather than relying on you remembering to include that in some big document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T07:47:48-07:00","id":1561971,"title":"","content":"How does the Privilege Pillar works?<br /> <br /> Say in our domain the Blood Sorcery use is prohibited with a Proscription that forces -4 to any rolls of Blood Sorcery in a domain (except one district that belongs to Acolits).<br /> <br /> Still some sorcerers get the License to work their blood rituals. The license is a Privilege that allows them to cast in any part of domain, outside the district. This Privilege lets your character ignore penalties up to -2.<br /> <br /> The question: will the licensed sorcerer get 0 penalty from the Anti-sorcerous Law and may ignore up to -2 from the other factors? Or the Privilege just lets him ignore -2 from the -4 of the Proscription?<br /> <br /> If the first option is right, will the Privilege benefit (ignore -2 from other penalties) work in the Acolite-district?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 07-20-2026, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}